  "title": "Everything you know about 2 is wrong?",
  "body": "Everything you know about 2 is wrong?   For all , .  We give the flawed proof and then explain what is wrong with it in the solutions below.   We prove this by induction. So let and assume that the statement is true for . That is Then we can write, by adding to both sides of the above inequality And thus the statement is true for . By mathematical induction, the statement is true for all .     This proof of the inductive step is perfectly correct. We have correctly shown that for all .  However, this is a vacuous statement, since the hypothesis is never true. This is the flaw in our proof we did not check the base-case. When , the statement is false.  Since the base case fails, we cannot use mathematical induction. Both the base case and the inductive step must be true for an induction proof to work.   "
